[center][color=#58D1B2][size=5][b]AIM - Alternative Installer for Mistria[/b][/size][/color][/center]
[b][color=#58D1B2][size=4]About AIM[/size][/color][/b]
[color=#F3EEE7]AIM is an independently maintained, open-source mod installer for [b]Fields of Mistria[/b]. It is a fork of MOMI, developed under a separate name with an enhanced user interface and additional compatibility and safety features.[/color]
[color=#F3EEE7]AIM is not intended to replace [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fieldsofmistria/mods/78]MOMI[/url]. If MOMI eventually provides the features and fixes maintained by AIM, this project may become unnecessary.[/color]
[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Features[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Self-contained single-executable packages for Windows, Linux/SteamOS, and macOS. No separate .NET installation is required.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#58D1B2]Automatic detection of the Fields of Mistria installation folder.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#B8AEA3]Automatic detection of nearby [b]mods[/b], [b]Mods[/b], or [b]MODS[/b] folders.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#58D1B2]Support for extracted mod folders and ZIP, RAR, and 7z archives.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Profiles for different mod configurations.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#B8AEA3]Search by mod name, author, description, or version; filtering never changes the saved mod order.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#B8AEA3]Drag-and-drop mod ordering with a visible insertion position and automatic scrolling for long mod lists.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Installation and uninstallation with archive backups, validation, and rollback protection.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#C05C46]Compatibility warnings for legacy GML, hooks, seams, shared files, and keyboard shortcuts.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#58D1B2]Nexus [b]Vortex[/b] button support through [b]nxm://[/b] links.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#58D1B2]Nexus update checks, update notifications, backups, rollback, and version freezing.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Automatic monitoring of the selected mods folder.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#B8AEA3]Load-order suggestions plus an on-demand, copyable issue report with exact shared files and compatibility details.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Optional direct game launching or Steam launching.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#58D1B2]Localized user interface with multiple language options.[/color][/*]
[/list]
[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size][/color]
[list=1]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Download the ZIP archive for your operating system.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Extract the archive to any folder of your choice.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Start the executable for your system:[/color][/*]
[/list]
[code]Windows: AIM.exe
Linux / SteamOS: AIM-linux
macOS: AIM-osx[/code]
[color=#F3EEE7]AIM will try to detect the game installation and a nearby mods folder automatically. You can also select or change both folders manually from Settings.[/color]
[color=#F6C177][b]Important:[/b] The Nexus ZIP archives contain one self-contained executable. Do not run the executable directly from inside the ZIP archive; extract it first.[/color]
[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Adding and Installing Mods[/b][/size][/color]
[list=1]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Place extracted mod folders or ZIP/RAR/7z archives in your selected mods folder. You can also use the Nexus [b]Vortex[/b] button ([b]nxm://[/b]); AIM downloads and unpacks the mod into the selected mods folder.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]AIM will detect available mods automatically.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Select the mods you want to keep active and press [b]Install[/b].[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Review any compatibility or conflict warnings before continuing.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Use [b]Uninstall All[/b] when replacing or testing a different mod set if you want a clean rebuild.[/color][/*]
[/list]
[color=#F6C177][b]Language mods:[/b] Language mods often modify shared localization files. AIM warns when selected mods share files. Usually install only one language mod at a time unless you have verified that the selected language mods are compatible.[/color]
[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Nexus Integration[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]AIM can check individual mods, selected mods, or the complete mod list for updates.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Manually installed mods can be associated with their Nexus page for update checks.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Updated mods keep a backup of the previous version and can be restored when necessary.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Nexus update features may require a personal Nexus API key configured in the AIM settings.[/color][/*]
[/list]
[color=#F6C177][b]Note:[/b] The public Nexus application/OAuth registration is currently awaiting approval. Until then, Nexus update features may require a personal Nexus API key configured in AIM settings.[/color]
[color=#F6C177][b]Older local installations:[/b] Mods installed before AIM 0.1.5 may not have an exact Nexus file identity recorded. Associate them manually before using update checks.[/color]
[color=#58D1B2][size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Fields of Mistria 1.0.4 and later 1.0.x versions.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Windows x64.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]Linux x64 / SteamOS x64.[/color][/*]
[*][color=#F3EEE7]macOS x64.[/color][/*]
[/list]
